  "headline": "Westpac's expense to income ratio (excluding Notable Items) rose 2.75ppt to 53.04% in FY25 from 50.29% in FY24. The deterioration was driven by operating expenses growing 9% ($10,944m to $11,916m) while operating income grew only 3% ($21,763m to $22,464m). Expense growth was led by a $273m Fit for Growth restructuring charge, $399m in UNITE investment spend, higher staff costs (+$397m, +7% driven by wage growth and investment in bankers), and technology costs (+$146m, +13% driven by UNITE and software amortisation), partially offset by $402m of productivity savings. Income growth of 3% came from net interest income (+3%) and non-interest income (+5%).",
